[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Cost of Government]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.73]Lesson 36 | 第36课
[00:03.66]The cost of government | 政府的开支
[00:11.16]What's the most important factor, both in government or business, for keeping running costs low? | 无论在政府还是企业中，使运转成本保持在低水平的最重要因素是什么？
[00:21.57]If a nation is essentialy disunited, it is left to the government to hold it together. | 如果一个国家基本上是分裂的，就只能靠政府把它团结起来。
[00:27.97]This increases the expense of government, and reduces correspondingly the amount of economic resources that could be used for developing the country. | 这就增加了政府的开支，相应地减少了本可以用于发展国家的经济资源。
[00:39.42]And it should not be forgotten how small those resources are in a poor and backward country. | 而且不应忘记，在一个贫穷落后的国家里，这些资源是多么微薄。
[00:45.74]Where the cost of government is high, resources for development are correspondingly low. | 政府的开支越大，用于发展的资源就越少。
[00:52.66]This may be illustrated by comparing the position of a nation with that of a private business enterprise. | 这可以通过把国家的处境同私营企业的处境相比较来说明。
[00:59.84]An enterprise has to incur certain costs and expenses in order to stay in business. | 企业为了维持经营必须支付一定的成本和费用。
[01:06.88]For our purposes, we are concerned only with one kind of cost--the cost of managing and administering the business. | 就我们的目的而言，我们只关心一种成本——经营管理企业的成本。
[01:15.36]Such administrative overheads in a business are analogous to the cost of government in a nation. | 企业的这种管理费用（行政开支）与一个国家的政府费用相类似。
[01:22.53]The administrative overheads of a business are low to the extent that everyone working in the business | 一个企业中每个人的行为
[01:28.21]can be trusted to behave in a way that best promotes the interests of the firm. | 能否被信赖是以最有利于公司的方式行事的，行政开支就低到这种程度。
[01:34.06]If they can each be trusted to take such responsibilities, | 如果他们每个人都能够被信赖承担起这种责任，
[01:37.79]and to exercise such initiative as falls within their sphere, then administrative overheads will be low. | 并在其职权范围内发挥这种主动性，那么行政开支就会是低的。
[01:46.41]It will be low because it will be necessary to have only one man looking after each job without having another man to check upon what he is doing, | 行政开支之所以低，是因为每一项工作只需一个人照管，而不需要另一个人去检查他的工作，
[01:56.06]keep him in line, and report on him to someone else. | 督促他守规矩，并向别人汇报他的情况。
[02:00.59]But if no one can be trusted to act in a loyal and responsible manner towards his job, | 但是，如果谁也不能被信赖以忠诚负责的态度对待本职工作，
[02:06.88]then the business will require armies of administrators, checkers and foremen and administrative overheads will rise correspondingly. | 那么企业就需要一大批行政人员、检查员和工头，行政开支也会相应上升。
[02:16.66]As administrative overheads rise, so the earnings of the business after meeting the expense of administration, will fall; | 随着行政开支的上升，企业在支付了管理费用之后的盈利就会下降；
[02:24.76]and the business will have less money to distribute as dividends or invest directly in its future progress and development. | 企业用于分红或直接投资于未来进展和发展的钱也就少了。
[02:32.86]It is precisely the same with a nation. | 国家的情况也完全一样。
[02:36.06]To the extent that the people can be relied on to behave in a loyal and responsible manner, | 在人民可以被信赖会以忠诚负责的态度行事的范围内，
[02:42.17]the government does not require armies of police and civil servants to keep them in order. | 政府就不需要大批的警察和文职人员来维持秩序。
[02:48.60]But if a nation is disunited, the government cannot be sure that the actions of the people will be in the interests of the nation; | 但是，如果国家是分裂的，政府就不能肯定人民的行动会符合国家的利益；
[02:57.21]and it will have to watch, check, and control the people accordingly. | 于是政府就不得不相应地监视、检查和控制人民。
[03:02.36]A disunited nation therefore has to incur unduly high costs of government. | 因此，一个分裂的国家不得不承担过高的政府开支。
